Article 17
(1) Prevention of violence against women and children is carried out in an integrated manner by the Regional Government coordinated by regional apparatus that has the main duties and functions of coordination in the field of women's empowerment and child protection.
(2) Prevention efforts as referred to in paragraph (1) are implemented by:
a. establishing a working network in violence prevention efforts;
b. conducting coordination, integration, synchronization of violence prevention based on partnership patterns;
c. providing counseling/guidance;
d. conducting socialization regarding laws and regulations related to the protection of women and child victims of violence; and
e. providing critical education on the rights of women and children for the community.

Article 18
(1) Prevention of the occurrence of violence against women and children as referred to in Article 17 shall be implemented by Regional Apparatus and UPTD whose main duties and functions are in the fields of:
a. education;
b. health;
c. social affairs;
d. labor;
e. women's empowerment and child protection; and
f. public peace and order.
(2) Prevention of the occurrence of violence by Regional Apparatus and UPTD as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be implemented in an integrated and continuous manner based on technical guidelines in the Regional Action Plan.

Article 16
In efforts to protect victims, the community and family have the following obligations and responsibilities:
a. prevent the occurrence of violence against women and children;
b. report if violence occurs;
c. protect victims; and
d. provide emergency assistance.

CHAPTER III
VIOLENCE
Article 5
Forms of violence against women and children include:
a. physical violence;
b. psychological violence;
c. sexual violence;
d. neglect;
e. exploitation; and/or
f. other violence.
- 7­

Article 21
(1) Complaint, consultation, and counseling services as referred to in Article 20 letter a shall be conducted by UPTD-PPA to follow up on reports of acts of violence against women and children submitted by victims, families or the community.
(2) Services as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be in the form of:
a. interviews and observation of the victim's condition;
b. initial identification or recording of the victim;
c. consent for action to be taken;
d. recommendation for follow-up services;
e. coordination and referral to follow-up services and related parties; and
f. administration of the complaint process.

Article 34
(1) In order to ensure the effectiveness of the implementation of KLA development policy in the Region, a KLA Task Force shall be established.
(2) The KLA Task Force as referred to in paragraph (1), shall have the following principal duties, namely:
 a. coordinating the implementation of KLA policy and development;
 b. determining the tasks of the members of the KLA Task Force;
 c. conducting socialization, advocacy and communication of information and education on KLA policy;
 d. collecting baseline data;
 e. conducting needs analysis sourced from baseline data;
 f. conducting dissemination of baseline data;
 g. determining the focus and priorities of programs in realizing KLA, which are adjusted to the potential of the Region;
 h. preparing a regional action plan and KLA working mechanism for 5 (five) years; and
 i. conducting monitoring, evaluation and reporting at least once every 1 (one) year.
(3) Further provisions regarding the procedures for appointment and dismissal of membership of the KLA Task Force shall be regulated by Regent Regulation.

Article 2
Protection of women and children victims of violence is conducted based on the principles of:
a. respect and fulfillment of victims' rights;
b. justice and gender equality;
c. non-discrimination;
d. best interests of victims; and
e. empowerment.

REGENT OF BUTON
PROVINCE OF SOUTHEAST SULAWESI
REGIONAL REGULATION OF BUTON REGENCY
NUMBER 6 YEAR 2021
CONCERNING
THE IMPLEMENTATION OF PROTECTION FOR WOMEN AND
CHILD VICTIMS OF VIOLENCE
BY THE GRACE OF ALMIGHTY GOD
THE REGENT OF BUTON,

Considering : a. that women and children are vulnerable groups who tend to experience acts of torture and violence and therefore must receive protection;
b. that to provide direction, foundation and legal certainty to all parties in the implementation of protection for women and children in Buton Regency, regulation is necessary;
c. that based on the considerations as referred to in letter a, and letter b, it is necessary to establish a Regional Regulation concerning the Implementation of Protection for Women and Child Victims of Violence;

Bearing in Mind 1. Article 18 paragraph (6) of the 1945 Constitution of the Republic of Indonesia;
2. Law Number 29 Year 1959 concerning the Establishment of Level II Regions in Sulawesi (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 1959 Number 74, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 1822);
3. Law Number 4 Year 1979 concerning Child Welfare (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 1979 Number 32, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3243);
4. Law Number 39 Year 1999 concerning Human Rights (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 1999 Number 165, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3835);
