Article 33
(1) The fulfillment of children's rights is implemented in an integrated and systematic manner across all sectors on an ongoing basis through KLA development policies.
(2) The KLA development policy as referred to in paragraph (1) contains provisions regarding:
 a. the KLA concept;
 b. children's rights; and
 c. the KLA development approach.
(3) The KLA development policy as referred to in paragraph (1) is directed at the fulfillment of children's rights, including:
 a. civil rights and freedoms;
 b. family environment and alternative care;
 c. basic health and welfare;
 d. education, use of leisure time, and cultural activities; and
 e. special protection.
(4) The stages of KLA development as referred to in paragraph (1) include:
 a. preparation;
 b. planning;
 c. implementation;
 d. monitoring;
 e. evaluation; and
 f. reporting.
(5) Further provisions regarding KLA development policy are regulated by Regent Regulation.
